From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:12:28 +0200
Subject: Give an inline accessor for a module the module's TermRef
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A module val's info is a TypeRef to its module class. An inline accessor
carrying that info is not a legal path, so any type selected through it —
`Positional.Profile`, where `Positional` is a qualified-private object used
from an inline method — is rejected by PostTyper's realizability check as
soon as the accessor cannot be final, which is the case whenever it lands in
a trait.

Remapping the accessor's info to the module's TermRef makes it stable again.
This restores the fix for scala/scala3#22593, which 5321891783 ("Don't infer
implicits from non-accessible companion", #25367) removed after its own
tests stopped needing it: that PR made the inaccessible-companion cases fail
earlier, for an unrelated reason, and dropped the remap along with them. The
type-selection case it also covered was left broken.

tests/pos/i22593c is that case: a type reached through an accessor for a
qualified-private module, expanded outside the defining package, with the
accessor hosted in a trait so it cannot be final. Soundness's `stratiform`
hits it in `Tel2.DecodableDerivation.conjunction`.

The tests touched by 5321891783 (tests/pos/i22593a, tests/pos/i22593b,
tests/pos/i25347, tests/neg/i22593a, tests/neg/i22593b, tests/neg/i25347,
tests/neg/i25347b) all still behave as marked under this patch.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (see LLM_POLICY.md)
Proscala-Patch: modulepath
---
 .../tools/dotc/transform/AccessProxies.scala  | 10 +++++++++-
 tests/pos/i22593c/Main.scala                  | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 tests/pos/i22593c/Test.scala                  |  3 +++
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/pos/i22593c/Main.scala
 create mode 100644 tests/pos/i22593c/Test.scala

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/AccessProxies.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/AccessProxies.scala
index 93d227937f6f3336035c1268beafa4e9e1f140a2..0b2fccc0bcd04a7a078988c8c42307d2fe3f6096 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/AccessProxies.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/AccessProxies.scala
@@ -154,8 +154,16 @@ abstract class AccessProxies {
         if accessorClass.is(Package) then
           accessorClass = ctx.owner.topLevelClass
         val accessorName = accessorNameOf(accessed.name, accessorClass)
+        val mappedInfo = accessed.info match
+          // A module val's info is a TypeRef to its module class, and an accessor
+          // returning that is not a legal path — so any type selected through the
+          // accessor (`Priv.Thing`) is rejected as unrealizable. Remap it to the
+          // module's TermRef, which is stable. See test i22593.scala (issue #22593).
+          case tref @ TypeRef(prefix, _) if tref.symbol.is(Module) =>
+            TermRef(prefix, tref.symbol.companionModule)
+          case other => other
         val accessorInfo =
-          accessed.info.ensureMethodic.asSeenFrom(accessorClass.thisType, accessed.owner)
+          mappedInfo.ensureMethodic.asSeenFrom(accessorClass.thisType, accessed.owner)
         val accessor = accessorSymbol(accessorClass, accessorName, accessorInfo, accessed)
         rewire(reference, accessor)
       }
diff --git a/tests/pos/i22593c/Main.scala b/tests/pos/i22593c/Main.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..13ed91adac6bf7f2ff197570e81ab6ba54489df5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos/i22593c/Main.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+// A type selected through an inline accessor for a qualified-private module.
+// The accessor's result type must be the module's TermRef; if it is the module
+// class's TypeRef instead, the accessor is not a legal path and every type
+// selected through it (`Positional.Profile`) is rejected as unrealizable.
+//
+// The accessor lands in `Host`, a trait, so it cannot be final — which is what
+// makes the realizability check depend on the result type being stable.
+package p
+
+private[p] object Positional:
+  class Profile(val name: String)
+
+trait Host:
+  object Derivation:
+    inline def make(): Int =
+      val profiles: Array[Positional.Profile] = Array(Positional.Profile("a"))
+      profiles.length
+
+object Instance extends Host
diff --git a/tests/pos/i22593c/Test.scala b/tests/pos/i22593c/Test.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1412f5a9d1c20af732a3497aee4a87fa9788402d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos/i22593c/Test.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+// Expanded outside `p`, so the accessor is really needed.
+object Test:
+  def run(): Int = p.Instance.Derivation.make()
